<figure class="acknowledgement" data-acknowledgement aria-labelledby="r38-ack-title">
 <p class="figure-title" id="r38-ack-title">Figure 1 · What is allowed to answer COMMIT?</p>
 <p class="note">Conceptual progression with one selected synchronous standby. Compare <em>on</em> and <em>remote_apply</em> at the remote-flush step.</p>
 <div class="copies"><div><strong>Primary</strong><p data-local data-live>WAL: earlier history</p></div><div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→ WAL →</div><div><strong>Selected standby</strong><p data-remote data-live>WAL: earlier history</p><p data-query data-live>Fresh read: no order 103</p></div></div>
 <p class="reply" data-reply data-live>Application waits</p><p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Purchase 103 has not committed. Both copies begin before the purchase.</p>
 <label>Commit requirement <select data-level><option value="local">local</option><option value="remote_write">remote_write</option><option value="on" selected>on</option><option value="remote_apply">remote_apply</option></select></label>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Commit acknowledgement playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span></div><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 <figcaption>The chosen setting moves the earliest permitted success reply. It does not make a different asynchronous standby participate or refresh an old query snapshot. File write and durable flush remain separate storage promises.</figcaption>
 <details><summary>Read the boundaries as text</summary><p>Every mode shown waits for the primary’s local flush. local adds no remote wait; remote_write waits for the selected standby’s file write; on waits for its durable flush; remote_apply waits for its replay. A fresh standby query includes 103 only after replay of the commit. With no configured synchronous standby set, all four modes shown have only the local wait.</p></details>
</figure>
<style>.acknowledgement{padding:1rem;margin:2rem 0;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.9rem/1.55 var(--font-sans)}.acknowledgement .figure-title{margin:0 0 1rem;font-size:1.1rem}.note,figcaption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.copies{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr;gap:.7rem;align-items:center}.copies>div:not(.arrow){padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);min-height:9rem}.copies p{margin:.6rem 0 0}.arrow{color:var(--color-accent);font-size:.8rem}.reply{padding:.7rem;border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);margin:1rem 0}.controls{display:flex;gap:.4rem;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin:1rem 0}button,select{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);padding:.45rem .65rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);border-radius:.2rem}button{cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}button[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}[data-hold]{height:3px;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;width:0;height:100%;background:var(--color-accent)}figcaption{margin:1rem 0}details p{margin-top:.8rem}@media(max-width:600px){.copies{grid-template-columns:1fr}.copies>div:not(.arrow){min-height:0}.arrow{text-align:center}}
</style>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-acknowledgement]')){
 const choice=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-level]')!;
 const remote=['earlier history','not yet received','written to OS cache','flushed through commit','commit replayed'];
 const text=['Purchase 103 has not committed. Both copies begin before the purchase.','The primary has flushed its commit. local can answer, although the standby has none of the new WAL yet.','The selected standby writes the WAL to its filesystem. remote_write can answer; a standby OS failure could still lose these unflushed bytes.','The standby flushes the commit. on can answer, even though a fresh query still cannot see the purchase.','The standby replays the commit. remote_apply can answer; a new enough snapshot on this copy can now see order 103.'];
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw:(n:number)=>{const threshold={local:1,remote_write:2,on:3,remote_apply:4}[choice.value]!;root.querySelector('[data-local]')!.textContent='WAL: '+(n?'commit flushed':'earlier history');root.querySelector('[data-remote]')!.textContent='WAL: '+remote[n];root.querySelector('[data-query]')!.textContent='Fresh read: '+(n===4?'order 103 present':'no order 103');root.querySelector('[data-reply]')!.textContent=n>=threshold?'Success permitted: '+choice.value:'Application waits: '+choice.value;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=text[n];}});
 choice.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
}
</script>
